        "content": "<p>A kernel-verified unconditional constant for the union-closed sets (Frankl) conjecture.</p>\n<p>The headline theorem, in <code>UCFrankl/DiagonalReduction.lean</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">franklWithConstant_psi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FranklWithConstant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">psi</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">psi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real.sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ≈ 0.38197</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FranklWithConstant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">UnionClosed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F.Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F.card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">freq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So: every finite union-closed family other than <code>{∅}</code> has an element contained in at least <code>ψ = (3-√5)/2</code> of its members — the Gilmer–Alweiss–Huang–Sellke / Chase–Lovett / Sawin–Pebody bound, <code>ψ</code> being the golden optimum of the one-step entropy method. As far as I know this is the first time this constant has been checked end-to-end by the Lean kernel with no open hypothesis. (The full Frankl conjecture is the <code>c = 1/2</code> case, <code>FranklConjecture</code>, and remains open — this is not a claim about it.)</p>\n<p>The reduction is factored so the analytic content sits in one scalar atom:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">franklWithConstant_psi_of_weakBoppana</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hWB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WeakBoppana</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boppanaConst</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">FranklWithConstant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">psi</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">weakBoppana_sharp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WeakBoppana</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">boppanaConst</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"c1\">-- boppanaConst = (1+√5)/4</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gilmerEngine_of_lt_psi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">psi</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GilmerEngine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Also formalized: <code>franklWithConstant_centile : FranklWithConstant (1/100)</code> (Gilmer's original constant, unconditional).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Toolchain <code>leanprover/lean4:v4.30.0</code>, mathlib pinned at tag <code>v4.30.0</code> (revs frozen in <code>lake-manifest.json</code>).</li>\n<li>Axiom audit via <code>scripts/CheckAxioms.lean</code> (<code>#print axioms</code> on every top-level result, incl. <code>franklWithConstant_psi</code>): only <code>propext</code>, <code>Classical.choice</code>, <code>Quot.sound</code> — no <code>sorryAx</code>, no <code>native_decide</code>, no extra axioms.</li>\n<li>Source + pinned manifests: <a href=\"https://github.com/demonstrandum-research/artifacts\">https://github.com/demonstrandum-research/artifacts</a></li>\n<li>Archived: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21264100\">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21264100</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The development was produced by an AI workflow (Demonstrandum); the Lean kernel is the guarantor, and I'd welcome scrutiny of the entropy-reduction layer (<code>EngineReduction.lean</code>, <code>HoBoppana.lean</code>, <code>DiagonalReduction.lean</code>) in particular.</p>\n<p>— John Erlbacher (Independent Researcher)</p>",
